REFERENCE   1  (bases 1 to 4560)
  AUTHORS   Li ZC, Zhai G, Zhang J, Wang Z, Liu G, Wu GY, Liang D and Zheng H.
  TITLE     Differentiation of clear cell and non-clear cell renal cell
            carcinomas by all-relevant radiomics features from multiphase CT: a
            VHL mutation perspective
  JOURNAL   Eur Radiol 29 (8), 3996-4007 (2019)
   PUBMED   30523454
  REMARK    GeneRIF: Most RCC-subtype-discriminative CT features were associated
            with the key RCC-driven gene-the VHL gene mutation.
REFERENCE   2  (bases 1 to 4560)
  AUTHORS   Chen G, Zhou J, Chen J, Zhu J, Liu SC, Ding XF and Zhang Q.
  TITLE     VHL regulates NEK1 via both HIF-2alpha pathway and
            ubiquitin-proteasome pathway in renal cancer cell
  JOURNAL   Biochem. Biophys. Res. Commun. 509 (3), 797-802 (2019)
   PUBMED   30635121
  REMARK    GeneRIF: These findings showed that VHL regulates NEK1 via both
            HIF-2alpha pathway and ubiquitin-proteasome pathway in renal cancer
            cells.
REFERENCE   3  (bases 1 to 4560)
  AUTHORS   Liu J, Wang Y, Wang S, Si H and Duan W.
  TITLE     [Mutation analysis for a family affected with von Hippel-Lindau
            syndrome]
  JOURNAL   Zhonghua Yi Xue Yi Chuan Xue Za Zhi 35 (6), 860-863 (2018)
   PUBMED   30512164
  REMARK    GeneRIF: A novel mutation was found in exon 2 of the VHL gene; the
            alpha-structure of pVHL is completely absent. The novel
            c.426delT(p.V142fs) mutation probably underlies von Hippel-Lindau
            syndrome in this pedigree.
